executionContract.intendedBehavior:
scripts/moe-agent.sh never hands claude (--print or TUI) or gemini (--print or --prompt-interactive) a user prompt larger than PROMPT_ARGV_MAX_BYTES (100000, counted in bytes) as one argv string.
Above that, the wrapper:
- writes the prompt byte for byte to a private 0600 file made by mktemp in its 0700 SECURE_TEMP_DIR;
- puts moe-agent.ps1's read directive on argv in its place;
- prints '[prompt-overflow] prompt routed via private session context file: <N> bytes > 100000-byte argv limit.';
- deletes the file right after the CLI exits (cleanup_temp covers every other exit).
Prompts of 100000 bytes or less reach argv byte-identical, so prompt-cache replay is unchanged.
If the file cannot be written, the wrapper exits 1 with an [ERROR] line and never passes the oversize argv.
